title: In a subscribee folder, deleting one's fork drawn in a member's place still hides the member, as before.
pid: 21d9d790-560a-49b2-a295-afd3d0d84915
body: |2-
  The subscriber whose folder it is is the user's, so the old reading
  stands: the deletion removes the member from what the subscriber
  shows, which is a hide. Nor does such a deletion file the member,
  though it is an edit "written in" it. The other way: let the
  deletion dismiss nothing, so that taking back a reply in the unread
  list leaves the message unread; built first, and taken out with the
  owned-parent case above, for the same reason.
